20. Practical Risk Management Workflow
1. Define the trading or investment strategy.
2. Identify the major risks and conditions that invalidate the plan.
3. Determine available capital and acceptable loss limits.
4. Set the maximum risk per trade or investment.
5. Calculate position size before entering.
6. Account for fees, taxes, spread and possible slippage.
7. Define the stop-loss, exit rules or investment review criteria.
8. Check total portfolio exposure and correlated positions.
9. Confirm margin and liquidity requirements, if applicable.
10. Execute according to the plan.
11. Monitor risk and avoid unplanned increases in exposure.
12. Record the result in a journal.
13. Review performance and adjust risk rules based on evidence.
